    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Warner Reprise Years is a lavish 9LP box set by the American new wave band the B-52's, released on June 20, 2025, by Rhino Records to chronicle their prolific era with Warner Records and Reprise Records from 1979 to 1992. This comprehensive collection features the band's complete studio output during this period, including their self-titled debut, Wild Planet, Mesopotamia EP, Party Mix!, Whammy!, Bouncing Off the Satellites, the massively successful Cosmic Thing, and Good Stuff, with Good Stuff presented as a double LP to complete the nine-disc count . The vinyl edition is a limited release of 2,000 copies, distinguished by its \"rainbow\" aesthetic where each album is pressed on uniquely colored, swirled, or splattered vinyl, ranging from the yellow debut to the purple double-LP of Good Stuff .\n\nMusically, the box set captures the B-52's evolution from cult favorites to unlikely hitmakers, showcasing their vibrant blend of Rock and Pop infused with 50s and 60s pop influences, rock & roll, and campy kitsch culture . The collection includes the band's most iconic megahits, such as \"Rock Lobster,\" \"Private Idaho,\" \"Love Shack,\" and \"Roam,\" alongside classics that defined their free-spirited musical style . Notably, the set excludes the 2008 album Funplex because it was released on Astralwerks Records rather than Warner or Reprise, making this compilation a nearly complete archive of their label tenure . While the albums are presented in their original, non-expanded forms without bonus tracks, the set serves as the ultimate party collection for fans, featuring newly remastered audio on an array of colored discs and vinyl .",
